.TH GET_KRB_PRINCIPAL.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
get_krb_principal.sh \- export KRB5_PRINCIPAL from the active ticket cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source get_krb_principal.sh
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B get_krb_principal.sh
finds the FNAL.GOV Kerberos principal in the credential cache the
current shell logged in with, and exports it as
\fBKRB5_PRINCIPAL\fR.
.PP
Only FNAL.GOV principals are considered, since that is the realm the
Mu2e DAQ accounts live in. \fBklist \-l\fR is tried first; if that
build of krb5 does not support cache collections, the default cache's
principal is used instead, and is still required to be in FNAL.GOV.
.PP
.B This script should be sourced,
so the export persists in the calling shell. Executed directly it
prints the principal instead, which is useful in a pipeline.
.PP
.BR set_git_env.sh (1)
consumes \fBKRB5_PRINCIPAL\fR to derive the git identity, so this
script runs first in the login sequence.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Do not warn when no principal can be found. The non-zero return status
still reports it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and return.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRB5_PRINCIPAL
Set by this script on success.
.TP
.B KRB5CCNAME
Honoured indirectly through \fBklist\fR. The installed
\fI~/.bashrc\fR rewrites it to a randomised path when the cache belongs
to a shared group account, so shifters on one node do not share
credentials.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when a principal was found and exported, 1 when \fBklist\fR
is unavailable or no FNAL.GOV principal is in the cache, and 2 for an
unrecognised option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set the principal for this shell:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source get_krb_principal.sh
echo "$KRB5_PRINCIPAL"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read it without touching the environment:
.PP
.RS
.nf
principal=$(get_krb_principal.sh)
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR get_krb_daq_principal.sh (1),
.BR set_git_env.sh (1),
.BR setup-online.sh (1),
.BR klist (1),
.BR kinit (1)
